[Desktop Entry]
Name=Gowl
Comment=A GObject-based Wayland compositor inspired by dwl and dwm
# Do NOT `exec' gowl: when the compositor exits -- cleanly OR by crash --
# the surviving shell stops the session target gowl pulled in
# (gowl-session.target -> graphical-session.target).  Otherwise the
# persistent user@ manager keeps graphical-session.target active and the
# next login (even GNOME) aborts with "A graphical session is already
# running!", wedging all logins until reboot.  Best-effort (|| true).
Exec=/bin/sh -c 'gowl; systemctl --user stop gowl-session.target graphical-session.target 2>/dev/null || true'
Type=Application
Icon=gowl
# XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP for the session.  Order is load-bearing, and each
# name is here for a different consumer:
#
#   gowl     -- xdg-desktop-portal reads <desktop>-portals.conf, and the
#               gowl InputCapture/RemoteDesktop backend carries UseIn=gowl.
#   wlroots  -- matches xdg-desktop-portal-wlr's UseIn
#               (wlroots;sway;Wayfire;river;phosh;Hyprland), so screen-share
#               apps get the wlroots ScreenCast portal.  Without it the
#               portal frontend finds no ScreenCast backend and the share
#               picker does nothing.
#   GNOME    -- LAST, and only as a fallback for software that pattern-matches
#               this variable against a hardcoded list of desktops it knows.
#
# That last one is not cosmetic.  Chromium (and therefore every Electron
# app) picks its password store by splitting XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP on ':'
# and comparing each name against a fixed set -- GNOME, KDE, XFCE, Unity,
# Cinnamon, Pantheon, UKUI, LXQt.  A session naming none of them resolves
# to DESKTOP_ENVIRONMENT_OTHER, and key_storage_util_linux then selects the
# PLAINTEXT backend instead of libsecret.  The user-visible symptom is an
# Electron app announcing it cannot save your session and you will have to
# log in again next time -- which is also what happens to secrets it had
# already stored under a session that did report GNOME, because the
# backend changed underneath them.
#
# GNOME goes last so every first-match consumer still resolves to gowl or
# wlroots: the portal picks gowl-portals.conf (the first name here with a
# matching <name>-portals.conf), and UseIn matching hits gowl and wlroots
# first.  gowl runs no XDG autostart .desktop files, so nothing here can
# trip an OnlyShowIn=GNOME entry.
DesktopNames=gowl:wlroots:GNOME
